{
    // The JSX/Solid half of the type-surface gate. Read
    // `scripts/check-type-surfaces.mjs` for what the halves prove; this file only
    // pins the four settings the half REQUIRES, and each one is proved
    // load-bearing by a `tsconfig.probe-*.json` beside it.
    //
    //  - `jsx: "preserve"` — what `babel-preset-solid` needs. `"react"` is refused
    //    outright with `jsxImportSource` (TS5089, probe `jsx-react`).
    //  - `jsxImportSource: "@gjsify/gtk-host"` — the spelling a consumer writes;
    //    TypeScript appends `/jsx-runtime`. The `paths` entry below is what makes
    //    that resolve to `src/` instead of to a BUILD output, so this gate needs
    //    no `gjsify run build` in front of it.
    //  - `noImplicitAny: true` — with `jsx: "preserve"` and no `jsxImportSource`,
    //    every JSX element is implicitly `any` and `tsc` exits 0 having checked
    //    nothing (probe `evaporate`).
    //  - `strictFunctionTypes: true` — without it a handler parameter is
    //    bivariant, so the generated GIR signatures stop being checkable
    //    (probe `bivariant`).
    "compilerOptions": {
        "noEmit": true,
        "target": "es2020",
        "module": "NodeNext",
        "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
        "skipLibCheck": true,
        "noImplicitAny": true,
        "strictFunctionTypes": true,
        "jsx": "preserve",
        "jsxImportSource": "@gjsify/gtk-host",
        // Resolves the package's own subpath to SOURCE. Without it TypeScript
        // follows the `exports` map into `lib/`, which is a build output — and a
        // STALE `lib/types` (measured: `lib/esm/jsx-runtime.js` present,
        // `lib/types/jsx-runtime.d.ts` absent) makes the whole surface an
        // implicit `any` for a reason that has nothing to do with the surface.
        // What this deliberately does NOT prove: that `package.json#exports`
        // carries a `./jsx-runtime` entry at all. That is `verify-package-outputs`.
        "paths": {
            "@gjsify/gtk-host/jsx-runtime": ["../../src/jsx-runtime.ts"]
        },
        "lib": ["es2015", "es2016", "es2017", "DOM"],
        "types": []
    },
    // Every `.tsx` beside this file EXCEPT the sentinel, which is a deliberate
    // error and has its own tsconfig. A file list that misses a fixture is the
    // vacuous-green shape this whole directory exists to refuse, so the glob is
    // wide and the exclusion is explicit.
    "include": ["*.tsx"],
    "exclude": ["sentinel.tsx"]
}
